Tamzen
======

Tamzen is a monospaced bitmap font by Suraj N. Kurapati
(https://github.com/sunaku/tamzen-font), a fork of Tamsyn by Scott Fial
(http://www.fial.com/~scott/tamsyn-font/). TinyDev ships its sizes 8x15 and
8x16 (regular) as an AmigaOS font (Tamzen 15 and 16), limited to
ISO-8859-1. The glyphs Tamzen lacks there (section, ordinals, not,
registered, macron, plus-minus, superscripts, acute, micro, pilcrow, middle
dot, fractions) were drawn for TinyDev in 2026 by André Gewert; they are
free under the same terms.

The licence of Tamsyn and Tamzen follows, as distributed with Tamzen:


